<br>
Pro <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#cccb9b><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> <A HREF=http://pub50.ezboard.com/bgoldenlegion.showLocalUserPublicProfile?login=cyri>Cyri</A></span><br> <span class=usertitle>Registered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/25/01 10:06:39 am)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=41.topic&index=36>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> KK Raid</span><hr size=1> I'm game I want to check this place out.  Never been there before.  Anyone need some underwater breathing potions I can make some tonight.  Will have plenty of fish scales and my underwater breathing spell handy.  I have been reading a few guides about the dungeon and anyone who has lag spikes or a slow connection like myself could be dying a lot.  When you have a lag spike the underwater breathing spell is not working and you will drown.  Just thought I would add that little bit of info.<br>
<br>
Cya there<br>
<br>
Cyri <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#deddbf><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> <A HREF=http://pub50.ezboard.com/utressiasylvannis.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Tressia Sylvannis</A></span><br> <span class=usertitle>Registered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/26/01 9:04:51 am)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=41.topic&index=37>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> Re: KK Raid</span><hr size=1> Pro - so sorry to hear about your father-in-law, hope the surgery went well.<br>
<br>
Thanks to any guests and allies that have offered to come.  Hopefully you understand that the specifically sought after items (mermaid hair, item for shaman and paladin) will go to the quild members for which this raid was initially planned for.  For anything else I want to be fair to everyone, and am still pondering a +on rolls for anyone that has attended at least 2-3 prior raids, or that those people will get first dibs on rolls.  Again any $$ loot will be MLed and split among the groups.<br>
<br>
Until I get a feel for this dungeon again I am implementing again that we all *stay together*.  Also depending on size and number of groups and what we at first see we can handle we can possibly split up and camp different rooms.  If this happens any items looted will still be divvied and rolled for by everyone at lewt call (with the exception of specific class items which will be rolled for by those classes that need).<br>
<br>
I plan on this being about 6 hours (8pm cent to 2am cent)<br>
in the hopes that we can get our people the items they need.  <br>
<br>
On a side note - I see one of my priorities as *fairness to everyone* - so anything I do please know that is how I operate and am sometimes faced with a difficult decision that might require some input. <br>
